# ── Data: never commit student PII ─────────────────────────────
sample_data/
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.csv
*.duckdb
*.db
*.zip

# ── Secrets / keys: never commit ───────────────────────────────
.streamlit/secrets.toml
*.json
service_account*.json
credentials*.json
# `.env` under Python below only matches a file named EXACTLY that, so an
# `lms_api.env` copied in here would have been committed. The LMS key lives in
# the parent folder deliberately; this makes the repo refuse it either way.
*.env
# exception: aggregate-only data the app embeds (no PII, no secrets)
!intro_attendance.json

# ── Local speed cache (attendee bytes + marked-roster pickles) ─
.cache/
.lms_cache/

# ── LMS extracts: raw API payloads, every row of them student PII ──
# *.json already covers a plain dump, but a line-delimited or pickled cache
# (the shapes the parent folder's sweep scripts use) was covered by nothing.
*.jsonl
*.pkl
lms_extract*

# ── Derived-facts memo (aggregates only, but it belongs on the Drive) ─
# It lives in the private store folder, never here. These lines exist so a
# stray local copy cannot be committed: *.json already covers the uncompressed
# form, nothing covered *.gz.
*.gz
derived_facts*

# ── Generated website: /roster holds student contact details, never commit ─
site/
.vercel/

# ── Python ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
.env

# ── Misc ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
